# Per-session agent scratch space — dev-server and tunnel logs, throwaway HTML.
# Regenerable runtime noise, not project history.
.codex-temp/

# Claude Code's per-session git worktrees. Each is a complete second checkout
# with its own node_modules, and it does not inherit this file — so the Booqable
# sync scripts inside two of them still held the API token in plaintext for the
# six days after it was scrubbed from the main tree's history. Purged 8 Sep 2026;
# never track or keep them. See docs/STAGE_0.md S0-1 and RULINGS-2026-09-08 R-30.
# (graft/.cache, the other place the token sat, is already covered by /graft/.)
.claude/worktrees/

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
/graft/

# Plugin receipt telemetry — append-only, unsigned, written into whichever
# directory a tool happened to run in. Regenerable noise, not project history.
receipts/
review-receipts/

# The impeccable design hook's cache — per-session edit counts and "clean"
# acknowledgements, keyed by session id. Every concurrent session rewrites it,
# so a tracked copy turns each commit into a snapshot of whatever OTHER sessions
# happened to be editing at the time. Regenerable bookkeeping, not project history.
/.impeccable/

# `npm run check:lifecycle` writes this for `npm run completion` (R-29) to read
# and for the CI job to upload. It is a measurement of one run, not history.
.lifecycle-result.json

# The Docker-free local database and object store — `npm run db:local` and
# `npm run storage:local`. Postgres 18 (PGlite) on disk plus the bytes under
# .localdb/storage/. Rebuildable from supabase/migrations in one command, and
# it holds a copy of the seed corpus, so it is regenerable state, not history.
.localdb/

# Concurrent-session UI scratch (parse dumps, probe logs) and local packing archives
.tmp-ui-*/
tsc_check.txt
/babin-rentals-os md.rar

